Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
define
    rtFace code={
        r := Grokking[argument];
        x := *r["if"];
        modsOf(*x);
        };
    rtOwn code={
        r := RtReg[argument];
        modsOf(*r);
        };
    rtTerm code={
        r := RtReg[argument];
        x := *r["RtL"];
        modsOf(*x);
        };
    rtGrok code={
        r := Grokking[argument];
        modsOf(*r);
        };
    ;
register(RtReg);
define
    RtL="l";
    RtN="n";
    RtR    isRule RtL kz-="z";
    ;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities RtReg list;
cerr "RT-1 the keyword master `if`, read through IF's reference (they share one body)":;
rtFace("IF");
cerr "RT-2 a literal RtL referenced by the rule RtR -- its master, and RtR's reference":;
rtOwn("RtL");
rtTerm("RtR");
cerr "RT-3 a literal RtN referenced by nothing -- negative control":;
rtOwn("RtN");
cerr "RT-4 a punctuation master -- a rule by REGISTRATION in Grokking":;
rtGrok("leftBrace");
cerr "RULETERMT SENTINEL":;
stop();

ruleTermT -- OBJECT MODEL STROKE 2: "THIS TERM TAKES PART AS A RULE TERM" IS A FACT ABOUT THE REFERENCE, NOT
THE RULE.

Attaching a copy under a rule used to set isRule on the BODY the copy shares with its master, so the keyword
masters in Keywords (if, do, while, ...) read as defined rules because some rule mentioned them. After stroke 2
the copy's own rStuff carries ruleTerm; the body's isRule is written at definition only; readers that ask the
instance meaning ask isRuleTerm() (instance, then body -- today's union), rule readers read the body.

RT-1  IF's reference to `if` -- one body with the Keywords/if master: want bodyIsRule 0 (trunk 1, the leak),
      isRuleTerm 1 (it still takes part as a rule term).
RT-2  RtL's master: bodyIsRule 0 (trunk 1). RtR's reference to RtL: bodyIsRule 0, isRuleTerm 1.
RT-3  RtN, referenced by nothing: 0 and 0 on both builds (negative control).
RT-4 a punctuation master -- a rule by REGISTRATION in Grokking":;
rtGrok("leftBrace");
cerr "RULETERMT SENTINEL":;
stop();

